<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9260] StandaloneWalRecordsIterator broken on WalSegmentTailReachedException not in work dir</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9260</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;After implementation &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9050&quot; title=&quot;WALIterator should throw an exception if iterator stopped in the WAL archive but not in WAL work&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9050&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9050&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, StandaloneWalRecordsIterator became broke because in the standalone mode we can stop the iteration at any moment when the last available segment will be fully read.  And validation which was implemented in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9050&quot; title=&quot;WALIterator should throw an exception if iterator stopped in the WAL archive but not in WAL work&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9050&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9050&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is not applicable for standalone mode. Need to change behavior and validate what we stop an iteration in last available WAL segment.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13178707">IGNITE-9260</key>
            <summary>StandaloneWalRecordsIterator broken on WalSegmentTailReachedException not in work dir</summary>
